※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=5302
※ pl4g-test: args -shared
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 5302 LANG_HOST_RESULT_TYPE

※ What a function the host defines answers with is nothing, a number, a record
※ laid out for C, or a `str`, which the program copies out of the host's text
※ before the call returns.  A list would be memory the host made, laid out as
※ nothing in C is, and nothing here could say how long it lasts or who gives
※ it back; and text inside a result is not text the crossing copies, which
※ copies a `str` answered as itself and nothing holding one.

@[host("words")]
fn words(name: str) → [u64]

@[host("getenv")]
fn getenv(name: str) → str ? i32

@[visible, cdecl, impure]
fn run() → i64:
    0i64
